 # Code Review
@@ -64,6 +66,34 @@ user commit unaware that open findings exist.
 - `--fix`: after reporting, apply fixes for the confirmed findings directly to the working
   tree, then re-run the affected checks (typecheck/tests) to confirm the fix didn't break
   anything. Do not silently fix — tell the user what was changed and why.
+- `--commit`: runs **last**, after the report and after `--fix` (if given). Creates **one
+  local commit** of the reviewed diff, only if every gate below holds. If any gate fails, do
+  **not** commit — say which gate failed and why, and leave the next move to the user.
+  - **Gates** (all required):
+    1. There is something to commit. An empty or trivial diff means nothing to do (see Rules).
+    2. No confirmed finding is left open — each one was fixed. If any remains, warn as in
+       Step 3 and stop. So `--commit` without `--fix` only commits when nothing was found.
+    3. After the fixes, the checks the project requires before committing — as its
+       `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` states (e.g. agent-code: `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`,
+       `npm run build`) — were run and passed. If it documents none, run the typecheck/tests
+       the project has and say which ran. A check that could not run (missing tool, etc.)
+       counts as **failed**, not passed.
+  - **What goes in**: the whole reviewed diff — the original work plus the fixes — limited to
+    the Step 1 scope: the files of the task under review. Anything unrelated in the tree
+    (even if already staged) stays out; list what you left out. Stage by explicit path only,
+    never `git add -A` / `git add .` (other agents may be working in the same tree). Never
+    commit `.env`, credentials or secrets; if one is in scope, leave it out and say so.
+    Sequence: `git status --short`, then
+    `git add -- <untracked paths in scope>`, then `git commit -m "<msg>" -- <every path in
+    scope>`. Passing paths commits exactly those paths and ignores anything else already
+    staged (`--only`, git's default with paths).
+  - **Message**: Conventional Commits, in the language of the repo history (check `git log`),
+    plus any commit rule in the project's `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`. No `Co-Authored-By` trailer
+    unless the project's `.claude/settings.json` sets `attribution.commit`.
+  - **Where**: the current branch. No push, no new branch, no `--amend`, no `--no-verify` — if
+    a hook rejects the commit, report it instead of bypassing.
+  - **Finally**: report the commit hash and message (`git log -1 --oneline`), or the gate that
+    blocked it.
 
